     server's data/XML/vocations.xml between "BEGIN chaos vocations" / "END chaos vocations" markers (idempotent).

     ids 11-13 follow the base server's 0-10 (9/10 Illusionist / Arch Illusionist).
     Ninja and Samurai both have fromvoc="11": the engine knows one promotion per vocation, so the choice between the two
     is made by data/scripts/chaos/ascension.lua (!ascend ninja|samurai), never by the engine's promotion.

     clientid: the vocation byte of the login packet (0x9F). 6 is the client's free sixth slot; Ninja and Samurai send
     16 and 26 so the client can tell all three apart (client/base-patches/0016-chaos-vocation-ids.patch maps
     6 -> 11, 16 -> 12, 26 -> 13; the other vocations keep sending their base slot).

     Gains per level, between the Knight (cap 25, hp 15, mana 5) and the Paladin (cap 20, hp 10, mana 15).
     attackspeed (ms per weapon swing; every other vocation 2000): with server/src-patches/0002 a weapon's own
     attackspeed is scaled by attackspeed / 2000, so the Thief line stays faster with any weapon.
     basespeed 230 (others 220). Skills: swords 1.1 like the Knight, distance 1.2 (shurikens), the other melee skills 1.3,
     magic level 2.0 (between the Paladin's 1.4 and the Knight's 3.0).
     formula meleeDamage / distDamage (weapon hits; every other vocation 1.0): Thief and Ninja 1.2, Samurai 1.3 (light
     one-handed blades against the Knight's two-handed weapons; measured in server/data/spells/README.md). The Samurai
     has defense / armor 1.1, the tankier ascended class. -->
